1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,330
Your head is older than your feet.

2
00:00:02,592 --> 00:00:03,935
Not a metaphor.

3
00:00:03,955 --> 00:00:06,205
Up there, time really runs faster.

4
00:00:06,801 --> 00:00:09,291
Einstein predicted it: gravity slows

5
00:00:09,311 --> 00:00:10,391
time down.

6
00:00:10,577 --> 00:00:12,207
The closer you are to Earth, the

7
00:00:12,227 --> 00:00:14,007
slower your clock ticks.

8
00:00:14,675 --> 00:00:17,175
In 2010, physicists measured it.

9
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:19,927
They lifted an atomic clock just 33

10
00:00:19,947 --> 00:00:21,057
centimeters...

11
00:00:21,304 --> 00:00:22,894
and it ticked faster.

12
00:00:23,591 --> 00:00:25,561
Your phone depends on this.

13
00:00:25,581 --> 00:00:28,711
Up in orbit, GPS clocks gain 38

14
00:00:28,731 --> 00:00:31,121
millionths of a second, every day.

15
00:00:31,416 --> 00:00:33,686
Light travels 11 kilometers in that

16
00:00:33,706 --> 00:00:34,396
time.

17
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:36,734
So every satellite is built to correct

18
00:00:36,754 --> 00:00:38,014
for Einstein.

19
00:00:38,981 --> 00:00:40,331
Now go down.

20
00:00:41,148 --> 00:00:43,378
Deep in the gravity well, the center

21
00:00:43,398 --> 00:00:45,278
of the Earth is about two and a half

22
00:00:45,298 --> 00:00:47,298
years younger than its surface.

23
00:00:48,493 --> 00:00:49,583
And you?

24
00:00:49,793 --> 00:00:52,373
Over a lifetime, your head gains a few

25
00:00:52,393 --> 00:00:54,383
hundred billionths of a second.

26
00:00:54,976 --> 00:00:55,946
Tiny.

27
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:57,413
But real.

28
00:00:57,856 --> 00:00:59,636
Which means, right now...
